  {
   "id": "soc.climate.agro-zones",
   "name": "Ethiopia's agro-climatic zones",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "An agro-climatic zone is land suited to a range of crops because of its climate. By altitude and temperature, Ethiopia has five traditional zones: Bereha (below 500 m, over 30°C), Qolla (500–1,500 m), Woina Dega (1,500–2,300 m), Dega (2,300–3,300 m) and Wurch (above 3,300 m, below 10°C)."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "በከፍታና ሙቀት መሠረት ኢትዮጵያ አምስት ባህላዊ ቀጠናዎች አሏት፤ በረሃ፣ ቆላ፣ ወይና ደጋ፣ ደጋ እና ውርጭ።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
